 {
  "text": "Welcome to the Brickell Mall. Today is a good day for shopping. Shirts are only twenty-nine ninety-nine. Ties are two for thirty dollars. Coffee at the café on the second floor is two fifty. We take cash and all cards. And remember: in Florida, the tax is not in the price. You pay it at the register. Thank you for shopping with us.",
  "voice": "ellen",
  "file": "a19_listening1.mp3"
 },
 {
  "text": "Hi, it's Paul. A small piece of advice about prices in the United States. The price in the store is not the final price. The tax comes at the end, at the register. In Miami, it is seven percent. So a shirt for thirty dollars is about thirty-two dollars. People say prices fast: nine ninety-nine, not nine dollars and ninety-nine cents. And almost everybody pays by card. Cash is OK, but small bills are better.",
  "voice": "arthur",
  "file": "a19_listening2.mp3"
 },
